/-!
# Dimension of the inverse image of a subvariety under a regular immersion or an lci morphism

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of varieties over a field and let `Z ⊆ Y` be a closed subvariety
of dimension `d`. This file proves the two bounds of Stacks tag 0AZN on the dimensions of the
irreducible components of the scheme-theoretic inverse image `f⁻¹(Z) = X ×_Y Z`: if `f` is a
regular immersion of codimension `c`, every component has dimension at least `d - c`, and if
`f` is a local complete intersection morphism of relative dimension `r`, every component has
dimension at least `d + r`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.IsLocalCompleteIntersectionOfRelativeDimension`: a morphism is a local
  complete intersection morphism of relative dimension `r` when it locally factors through a
  relative affine space by a Koszul-regular immersion, and every such factorization through
  `𝐀^J_Y` has conormal sheaf of rank `#J - r`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback_bounds`: **Stacks tag 0AZN**, both
  bounds in one statement, each under the hypotheses the source gives it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_le_component_pullback_add_of_isRegularImmersion`:
  **Stacks tag 0AZN, part (1)**, the codimension bound for a regular immersion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_add_relativeDimension_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback`:
  **Stacks tag 0AZN, part (2)**, the relative-dimension bound for a local complete intersection
  morphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_add`: the bound for an
  immersion whose stalk kernels need at most `c` generators, which is the local heart of both.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_le_of_conormal_rank`: an immersion whose conormal
  sheaf is finite locally free of rank `c` is cut out by `c` equations in every local ring.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_pullback_fst_le`: the generator bound on stalk
  kernels passes to the base change of a closed immersion along any morphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_closed_point_mem_unique_irreducibleComponent`: on a Noetherian scheme
  locally of finite type over a field, every irreducible component carries a closed point lying
  on no other component.
* `Stacks.Intersection.ringKrullDim_le_ringKrullDim_quotient_add_card`: the affine form, for a
  minimal prime over an ideal generated by `c` elements.

## Implementation notes

Dimensions are `topologicalKrullDim`, valued in `WithBot ℕ∞`, which has no subtraction; as
elsewhere in the dimension library the conclusion of part (1) is therefore written additively, as
`dim Z ≤ dim W + c`. The relative dimension of part (2) is an integer, negative for a regular
immersion, so there the two dimensions are produced as natural numbers — which they are, both
being transcendence degrees of residue fields over the base field — and the inequality
`d + r ≤ m` is stated in `ℤ`.

Being cut out by `c` equations is recorded as `(RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap x).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c`
at every point `x` of the source. This is what the dimension argument consumes, and it is weaker
than regularity of the cutting sequence: the lower bound on the dimension of a component needs
only an upper bound on the *number* of equations, not that they form a regular sequence.
`AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_add` is therefore stated
with that bound as a hypothesis and no regularity.

The codimension of a regular immersion is the rank of its conormal sheaf, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_le_of_conormal_rank` is the comparison supplying the
generator bound from it: the stalk of the conormal sheaf at `z` is the cotangent module `I/I²`
of the kernel `I` of the surjection of local rings
(`Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent`), so a conormal sheaf of rank `c` makes
`I/I²` free of rank `c`, hence `I/𝔪I` of dimension at most `c` over the residue field, hence `I`
generated by `c` elements by Nakayama. Nothing but the rank is used; regularity of the ideal
sheaf is carried in the statement of part (1) because the source carries it, not because the
proof needs it.

The base change from `f : X ⟶ Y` to `f⁻¹(Z) ⟶ Z` is the step from the local statement to the
tag. For a *closed* immersion `f` the inverse image is the fibre product `X ×_Y Z`, its
projection to `Z` is the base change of `f` and so is again a closed immersion, and the generator
bound transports because the stalk kernel of a base-changed closed immersion is the ideal
generated by the image of the original (`AlgebraicGeometry.ker_stalkMap_pullback_fst`), while
`Ideal.spanFinrank_map_le_of_fg` does not increase the number of generators. That last step needs
the original kernel to be finitely generated, which holds because `Y` is locally Noetherian; the
same hypothesis is what makes the generator bound a genuine constraint, since
`Submodule.spanFinrank` is `0` by convention on an ideal that is not finitely generated. A
general immersion `f` is factored as a closed immersion into the coborder neighbourhood `U` of
its image followed by the open immersion `U ⟶ Y`; the inverse image of `Z` is then the inverse
image, under that closed immersion, of the open subscheme `U ×_Y Z` of `Z`, which has the
dimension of `Z` because `Z` is irreducible.

Part (2) is the source's: a local factorization `U ⟶ 𝐀^J_Y ⟶ Y` of `f` by a Koszul-regular
immersion of codimension `c` turns the inverse image of `Z` over `U` into the inverse image of
`𝐀^J_Z` under that immersion, and `𝐀^J_Z` is an integral closed subscheme of `𝐀^J_Y` of
dimension `d + #J`. Part (1) applied there gives `d + #J ≤ dim W + c`, which is `d + r ≤ dim W`
since `#J = r + c`. The passage from a component of `f⁻¹(Z)` to a component of its restriction
to `U` is made at a closed point of the component lying on no other one, which is where the
choice of the chart is taken.

The affine form of the local statement is proved independently, and more sharply, from the
dimension formula for a finite type domain over a field together with Krull's height theorem; it
needs no closed point.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AZN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AZN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A21](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A21)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00P0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00P0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01R2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01R2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 069F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/069F)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u v

namespace Stacks.Intersection

/-- Let `T` be a finite type domain over a field and let `q` be a minimal prime over an ideal
generated by a finite set `s`. Then `dim T ≤ dim T ⧸ q + #s`: the height of `q` is at most `#s`
by Krull's height theorem, and heights add along the quotient by `q`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_le_ringKrullDim_quotient_add_card (k : Type u) [Field k] (T : Type v)
    [CommRing T] [IsDomain T] [Algebra k T] [Algebra.FiniteType k T] {s : Finset T}
    {q : Ideal T} [q.IsPrime] (hq : q ∈ (Ideal.span (s : Set T)).minimalPrimes) :
    ringKrullDim T ≤ ringKrullDim (T ⧸ q) + (s.card : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing T := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing k T
  rw [Stacks.Spectrum.LocalDimensionFormula.ringKrullDim_eq_height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient k T q,
    add_comm]
  gcongr
  exact_mod_cast Ideal.height_le_card_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_finset hq

/-- For a surjection `φ` of rings out of a Noetherian local ring whose kernel needs at most `n`
generators, `dim R ≤ dim S + n`. This is the iterated form of the statement that quotienting by
one element of the maximal ideal drops the dimension by at most one. -/
@[ega "IV 5.1.6" "partial"]
theorem ringKrullDim_le_ringKrullDim_add_of_surjective {R : Type u} {S : Type v} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Nontrivial S] (φ : R →+* S)
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (n : ℕ) (hspan : (RingHom.ker φ).spanFinrank ≤ n) :
    ringKrullDim R ≤ ringKrullDim S + (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  calc ringKrullDim R
      ≤ ringKrullDim (R ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) + ((RingHom.ker φ).spanFinrank : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
        ringKrullDim_le_ringKrullDim_quotient_add_spanFinrank _ <|
          IsLocalRing.ringJacobson_eq_maximalIdeal R ▸
            IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal (RingHom.ker_ne_top φ)
    _ ≤ ringKrullDim (R ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) + (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by gcongr
    _ = ringKrullDim S + (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
        rw [ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hφ)]

/-! ### Minimal numbers of generators over a local ring -/

/-- Over a local ring `A`, a module with a basis indexed by `Fin c` has `c`-dimensional
reduction modulo the maximal ideal. -/
theorem finrank_quotient_maximalIdeal_smul_of_basis
    {A M : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]
    {c : ℕ} (b : Module.Basis (Fin c) A M) :
    Module.finrank (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
      (M ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A M)) = c := by
  let K := A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A
  let bK : Module.Basis (Fin c) K (TensorProduct A K M) := b.baseChange K
  let e : (TensorProduct A K M) ≃ₗ[K]
      M ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A M) :=
    LinearEquiv.extendScalarsOfSurjective Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
      (TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul M (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A))
  rw [Module.finrank_eq_card_basis (bK.map e)]
  simp

/-- A module spanned by `c` elements over a local ring has at most `c`-dimensional reduction
modulo the maximal ideal. -/
theorem finrank_quotient_maximalIdeal_smul_le_of_span_range
    {A M : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] {c : ℕ}
    (v : Fin c → M) (hspan : Submodule.span A (Set.range v) = ⊤) :
    Module.finrank (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
      (M ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A M)) ≤ c := by
  let N : Submodule A M := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A M)
  have hw : Submodule.span A (Set.range (fun i => N.mkQ (v i))) = ⊤ := by
    calc Submodule.span A (Set.range (fun i => N.mkQ (v i)))
        = (Submodule.span A (Set.range v)).map N.mkQ := by
          rw [Submodule.map_span]
          congr 1
          ext x
          simp
      _ = ⊤ := by rw [hspan, Submodule.map_top, Submodule.range_mkQ]
  have hwK : Submodule.span (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
      (Set.range (fun i => N.mkQ (v i))) = ⊤ :=
    Submodule.span_eq_top_of_span_eq_top (R := A) (S := A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) _ hw
  simpa only [Fintype.card_fin] using finrank_le_of_span_eq_top hwK

/-- A module over a local ring `A` which is spanned over a quotient ring `B` of `A` acting
through the quotient map is spanned over `A` by the same family. -/
theorem span_eq_top_of_surjective_smul {A B M : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [Module B M] {φ : A →+* B} (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hsmul : ∀ (a : A) (m : M), φ a • m = a • m) {ι : Type*} (v : ι → M)
    (hspan : Submodule.span B (Set.range v) = ⊤) : Submodule.span A (Set.range v) = ⊤ := by
  refine le_antisymm le_top fun m hmTop => ?_
  clear hmTop
  have hm : m ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range v) := by rw [hspan]; trivial
  induction hm using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem m hm => exact Submodule.subset_span hm
  | zero => exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add a b _ _ iha ihb => exact Submodule.add_mem _ iha ihb
  | smul b a _ iha =>
      obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := hφ b
      rw [hsmul r a]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r iha

/-- A linear isomorphism carries a spanning family to a spanning family. -/
theorem span_range_map_eq_top {R M N : Type*} [Semiring R] [AddCommMonoid M] [Module R M]
    [AddCommMonoid N] [Module R N] (e : M ≃ₗ[R] N) {ι : Type*} (v : ι → M)
    (hv : Submodule.span R (Set.range v) = ⊤) :
    Submodule.span R (Set.range fun i => e (v i)) = ⊤ := by
  have h : (Set.range fun i => e (v i)) = e '' Set.range v := by
    ext x
    simp only [Set.mem_range, Set.mem_image]
    exact ⟨fun ⟨i, hi⟩ => ⟨v i, ⟨i, rfl⟩, hi⟩, fun ⟨y, ⟨i, hi⟩, hy⟩ => ⟨i, by rw [hi]; exact hy⟩⟩
  rw [h, Submodule.span_image_linearEquiv, hv, Submodule.map_top, LinearEquiv.range]

/-- For an ideal `I` of a local ring contained in the maximal ideal, the reduction of `I/I²`
modulo the maximal ideal is the reduction of `I` modulo the maximal ideal: the one is the
quotient of the other by a submodule already contained in `𝔪 · I`. -/
noncomputable def cotangentQuotientEquivQuotient {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (I : Ideal A) (hI : I ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    (I.Cotangent ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A I.Cotangent)) ≃ₗ[
        A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A]
      (I ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A I)) := by
  let m := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A
  let S : Submodule A I := I • (⊤ : Submodule A I)
  let T : Submodule A I := m • (⊤ : Submodule A I)
  let eA : ((I ⧸ S) ⧸ T.map S.mkQ) ≃ₗ[A] I ⧸ T :=
    Submodule.quotientQuotientEquivQuotient S T (Submodule.smul_mono_left hI)
  have hmap : T.map S.mkQ = m • (⊤ : Submodule A (I ⧸ S)) := by
    change Submodule.map S.mkQ (m • (⊤ : Submodule A I)) = m • (⊤ : Submodule A (I ⧸ S))
    rw [Submodule.map_smul'', Submodule.map_top, Submodule.range_mkQ]
  rw [hmap] at eA
  change ((I ⧸ S) ⧸ (m • (⊤ : Submodule A (I ⧸ S)))) ≃ₗ[A] I ⧸ (m • (⊤ : Submodule A I)) at eA
  refine { eA with map_smul' := ?_ }
  intro k z
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective k
  exact eA.map_smul a z

/-- **The minimal number of generators of the kernel of a surjection out of a Noetherian local
ring is read off from its cotangent module.** If `I/I²` is spanned by `c` elements over the
target, then `I` is generated by `c` elements. -/
theorem spanFinrank_ker_le_of_span_cotangent {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [CommRing B] [Nontrivial B] (φ : A →+* B)
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) {c : ℕ}
    [Module B (RingHom.ker φ).Cotangent]
    (hsmul : ∀ (a : A) (m : (RingHom.ker φ).Cotangent), φ a • m = a • m)
    (v : Fin c → (RingHom.ker φ).Cotangent)
    (hv : Submodule.span B (Set.range v) = ⊤) :
    (RingHom.ker φ).spanFinrank ≤ c := by
  have hne : RingHom.ker φ ≠ ⊤ := by
    rw [Ne, Ideal.eq_top_iff_one, RingHom.mem_ker, map_one]
    exact one_ne_zero
  rw [IsLocalRing.spanFinrank_eq_finrank_quotient _ (IsNoetherian.noetherian _),
    ← (cotangentQuotientEquivQuotient _ (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal hne)).finrank_eq]
  exact finrank_quotient_maximalIdeal_smul_le_of_span_range v
    (span_eq_top_of_surjective_smul hφ hsmul v hv)

end Stacks.Intersection

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Every irreducible component of a Noetherian scheme locally of finite type over a field
carries a closed point lying on no other irreducible component. -/
theorem exists_closed_point_mem_unique_irreducibleComponent (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (T : Scheme.{u}) (s : T ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] [IsNoetherian T]
    (W : Set T) (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents T) :
    ∃ x : T, IsClosed ({x} : Set T) ∧ x ∈ W ∧
      ∀ V ∈ irreducibleComponents T, x ∈ V → V = W := by
  classical
  have : JacobsonSpace T := LocallyOfFiniteType.jacobsonSpace s
  set others : Set (Set T) := {V | V ∈ irreducibleComponents T ∧ V ≠ W} with hothers
  have hothersClosed : IsClosed (⋃₀ others) :=
    (NoetherianSpace.finite_irreducibleComponents.subset fun _ hV => hV.1).isClosed_sUnion
      fun V hV => isClosed_of_mem_irreducibleComponents V hV.1
  have hηW : IsGenericPoint hW.1.genericPoint W :=
    hW.1.isGenericPoint_genericPoint_closure.trans
      (isClosed_of_mem_irreducibleComponents W hW).closure_eq
  have hηnot : hW.1.genericPoint ∉ ⋃₀ others := by
    rintro ⟨V, hV, hηV⟩
    have hWV : W ⊆ V := by
      rw [← hηW]
      exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hηV)
        (isClosed_of_mem_irreducibleComponents V hV.1)
    exact hV.2 (Set.Subset.antisymm (hW.2 hV.1.1 hWV) hWV)
  obtain ⟨x, hxgood, hxclosed⟩ :=
    nonempty_inter_closedPoints (Z := W \ ⋃₀ others) ⟨hW.1.genericPoint, hηW.mem, hηnot⟩
      ((isClosed_of_mem_irreducibleComponents W hW).isLocallyClosed.inter
        hothersClosed.isOpen_compl.isLocallyClosed)
  refine ⟨x, hxclosed, hxgood.1, fun V hV hxV => ?_⟩
  by_contra hne
  exact hxgood.2 ⟨V, ⟨hV, hne⟩, hxV⟩

/-- At a closed point lying on a single irreducible component, the dimension of that component
is the Krull dimension of the local ring. -/
theorem topologicalKrullDim_eq_ringKrullDim_stalk_of_unique_irreducibleComponent
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (T : Scheme.{u}) (s : T ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s]
    (W : Set T) (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents T) (x : T) (hxW : x ∈ W)
    (hxclosed : IsClosed ({x} : Set T))
    (hunique : ∀ V ∈ irreducibleComponents T, x ∈ V → V = W) :
    topologicalKrullDim W = ringKrullDim (T.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  rw [← topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_krullDimOfRing_stalk k T s x hxclosed,
    topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_iSup_irreducibleComponents k T s x,
    show {Z ∈ irreducibleComponents T | x ∈ Z} = {W} from
      Set.eq_singleton_iff_unique_mem.mpr ⟨⟨hW, hxW⟩, fun V hV => hunique V hV.1 hV.2⟩]
  simp

/-- The dimension of an integral scheme locally of finite type over a field is the Krull
dimension of its local ring at any closed point. -/
theorem topologicalKrullDim_eq_ringKrullDim_stalk_of_isIntegral (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (Z : Scheme.{u}) (s : Z ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] [IsIntegral Z] (z : Z)
    (hzclosed : IsClosed ({z} : Set Z)) :
    topologicalKrullDim Z = ringKrullDim (Z.presheaf.stalk z) := by
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_eq_topologicalKrullDimAt_of_irreducible k Z s z,
    topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_krullDimOfRing_stalk k Z s z hzclosed]

/-- The image of a closed point under an immersion into a scheme locally of finite type over a
field is again a closed point: the singleton is locally closed, and a Jacobson space has no
locally closed singleton that is not closed. -/
theorem isClosed_singleton_image_of_isImmersion (k : Type u) [Field k] {T Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (s : Z ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] (j : T ⟶ Z) [IsImmersion j] (x : T)
    (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set T)) : IsClosed ({j.base x} : Set Z) := by
  have : JacobsonSpace Z := LocallyOfFiniteType.jacobsonSpace s
  apply isClosed_singleton_of_isLocallyClosed_singleton
  rw [show ({j.base x} : Set Z) = j.base '' ({x} : Set T) by simp]
  exact hx.isLocallyClosed.image j.isEmbedding.isInducing IsImmersion.isLocallyClosed_range

/-- Let `Z` be an integral scheme locally of finite type over a field and let `j : T ⟶ Z` be an
immersion of a Noetherian scheme whose kernel on stalks is generated by at most `c` elements.
Then every irreducible component `W` of `T` satisfies `dim Z ≤ dim W + c`.

This is the local heart of Stacks 0AZN part (1), stated for a bare immersion `j` rather than for
a morphism and a pullback.  The tag itself is carried by
`topologicalKrullDim_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback_add` below, which instantiates
this at the base change `f⁻¹(Z) ⟶ Z` of a closed immersion `f : X ⟶ Y` along a subvariety
`Z ⊆ Y`.  No regularity of the cutting sequence is used or assumed, so the bound is more general
than the source's in that respect: only the number of equations matters. -/
theorem topologicalKrullDim_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_add (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {Z T : Scheme.{u}} (s : Z ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] [IsIntegral Z]
    [IsNoetherian T] (j : T ⟶ Z) [IsImmersion j] (W : Set T)
    (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents T) (c : ℕ)
    (hspan : ∀ x : T, (RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap x).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c) :
    topologicalKrullDim Z ≤ topologicalKrullDim W + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian Z := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian s
  obtain ⟨x, hxclosed, hxW, hunique⟩ :=
    exists_closed_point_mem_unique_irreducibleComponent k T (j ≫ s) W hW
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_eq_ringKrullDim_stalk_of_isIntegral k Z s (j.base x)
      (isClosed_singleton_image_of_isImmersion k s j x hxclosed),
    topologicalKrullDim_eq_ringKrullDim_stalk_of_unique_irreducibleComponent k T (j ≫ s) W hW x
      hxW hxclosed hunique]
  exact Stacks.Intersection.ringKrullDim_le_ringKrullDim_add_of_surjective
    (j.stalkMap x).hom (j.stalkMap_surjective x) c (hspan x)

/-- Precomposing a ring map with an isomorphism does not change the number of generators its
kernel needs: the kernel is carried across by the inverse isomorphism. -/
private lemma spanFinrank_ker_comp_of_isIso {R S T : CommRingCat.{u}} (e : R ⟶ S) [IsIso e]
    (φ : S ⟶ T) :
    (RingHom.ker (e ≫ φ).hom).spanFinrank = (RingHom.ker φ.hom).spanFinrank := by
  let ee : R ≃+* S := (asIso e).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  have h1 : RingHom.ker (e ≫ φ).hom = Ideal.comap ee (RingHom.ker φ.hom) := rfl
  rw [h1, ← Ideal.map_symm ee, Ideal.spanFinrank_map_eq_of_ringEquiv]

/-- **The number of equations cutting out a closed immersion survives a base change.** Let
`f : X ⟶ Y` be a closed immersion into a locally Noetherian scheme whose kernel on stalks needs
at most `c` generators, and let `g : Z ⟶ Y` be any morphism. Then the base change
`pullback.fst g f : Z ×_Y X ⟶ Z` is cut out of `Z` by at most `c` equations in the local ring at
every point: its stalk kernel is the ideal generated by the image of the stalk kernel of `f`,
and extending an ideal along a ring map does not increase the number of generators needed. -/
theorem spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_pullback_fst_le {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    (g : Z ⟶ Y) (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion f] (c : ℕ)
    (hspan : ∀ x : X, (RingHom.ker (f.stalkMap x).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c)
    (t : (pullback g f : Scheme.{u})) :
    (RingHom.ker ((pullback.fst g f).stalkMap t).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c := by
  rw [ker_stalkMap_pullback_fst g f t]
  refine le_trans (Ideal.spanFinrank_map_le_of_fg _ (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)) ?_
  rw [spanFinrank_ker_comp_of_isIso]
  exact hspan _

/-- A generator bound on the stalk kernels of `j` is a generator bound on those of `e ≫ j` for an
isomorphism `e`: the stalk map of an isomorphism is injective, so composing with it leaves the
kernel unchanged. -/
private lemma spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_comp_of_isIso_le {T' T Z : Scheme.{u}} (e : T' ⟶ T)
    [IsIso e] (j : T ⟶ Z) (c : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ t : T, (RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap t).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c) (t : T') :
    (RingHom.ker ((e ≫ j).stalkMap t).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c := by
  have key : RingHom.ker ((e ≫ j).stalkMap t).hom = RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap (e t)).hom := by
    have hc := Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp e j t
    rw [hc]
    exact RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _
      (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (e.stalkMap t)).1
  rw [key]
  exact h _

/-- A compact scheme locally of finite type over a field is Noetherian. -/
private lemma isNoetherian_of_compact_ofFiniteType {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {T : Scheme.{u}} (s : T ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] [CompactSpace T] :
    IsNoetherian T :=
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian T := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian s
  ⟨⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0AZN, part (1).** Let `Y` be a scheme locally of finite type over a
field `k`, let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a closed immersion whose kernel on stalks needs at most `c`
generators at every point, and let `i : Z ⟶ Y` exhibit `Z` as a subvariety of `Y`. Then every
irreducible component `W` of the scheme-theoretic inverse image `f⁻¹(Z) = X ×_Y Z` satisfies
`dim Z ≤ dim W + c`, that is, has dimension at least `dim Z - c`.

The projection of `f⁻¹(Z)` to `Z` is the base change of `f`, hence again a closed immersion cut
out by at most `c` equations at every point, and the bound for an immersion applies with `Z` as
the ambient integral scheme.

In the source the generator bound comes from `f` being a regular immersion of codimension `c`.
Only the bound is used by the dimension argument, and it is carried here as the hypothesis
`hspan`; `spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_le_of_conormal_rank` below supplies it from a conormal sheaf
of rank `c`, and
`topologicalKrullDim_le_component_pullback_add_of_isRegularImmersion` is the
tag itself. -/
theorem topologicalKrullDim_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback_add
    (k : Type u) [Field k] {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sY] (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion f] (i : Z ⟶ Y)
    [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsIntegral Z] [CompactSpace Z] (c : ℕ)
    (hspan : ∀ x : X, (RingHom.ker (f.stalkMap x).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c)
    (W : Set (pullback f i : Scheme.{u}))
    (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents (pullback f i : Scheme.{u})) :
    topologicalKrullDim Z ≤ topologicalKrullDim W + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian Y := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian sY
  have : CompactSpace ↥(pullback f i : Scheme.{u}) :=
    QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (pullback.snd f i)
  have : IsNoetherian (pullback f i : Scheme.{u}) :=
    isNoetherian_of_compact_ofFiniteType (pullback.snd f i ≫ (i ≫ sY))
  exact topologicalKrullDim_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_add k (i ≫ sY)
    ((pullbackSymmetry f i).hom ≫ pullback.fst i f) W hW c
    (spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_comp_of_isIso_le _ _ c
      (fun t => spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_pullback_fst_le i f c hspan t))

/-! ### The number of equations cutting out a regular immersion -/

attribute [local instance] Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkModule
  Stacks.Conormal.stalkMapAlgebra Stacks.Conormal.cotangentStalkModule

/-- The stalk at `z` of a sheaf of modules on a scheme that is finite locally free of rank `c`
has a basis indexed by `Fin c`, over the module structure of [Stacks, Tag 01CB]. -/
theorem nonempty_basis_stalk_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank {Z : Scheme.{u}} (F : Z.Modules)
    (c : ℕ) (hc : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F c) (z : Z) :
    Nonempty (Module.Basis (Fin c) (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) F.val.presheaf z))) := by
  have hc' : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := structureSheafRing Z.toRingedSpace) F c := hc
  have h := nonempty_stalkBasis_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank (X := Z) F c hc' z
  rwa [Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule_eq Z.toRingedSpace F.val z] at h

/-- The stalk at `z` of a sheaf of modules on a scheme that is finite locally free of rank `c`
is spanned by `c` elements over the local ring at `z`. -/
theorem exists_span_range_stalk_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank {Z : Scheme.{u}} (F : Z.Modules)
    (c : ℕ) (hc : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F c) (z : Z) :
    ∃ v : Fin c → ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) F.val.presheaf z),
      Submodule.span (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z)) (Set.range v) = ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨b⟩ := nonempty_basis_stalk_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank F c hc z
  exact ⟨⇑b, b.span_eq⟩

/-- **A regular immersion of codimension `c` is cut out by `c` equations in every local ring.**
If the conormal sheaf of an immersion `j` into a locally Noetherian scheme is finite locally
free of rank `c`, then the kernel of `𝒪_{coborder, j z} ⟶ 𝒪_{Z,z}` needs at most `c`
generators. -/
theorem spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_le_of_conormal_rank {Z X : Scheme.{u}}
    (j : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion j] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (c : ℕ)
    [hc : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf j) c]
    (z : Z) : (RingHom.ker (j.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c := by
  let : Module (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (RingHom.ker (j.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).Cotangent :=
    Stacks.Conormal.cotangentStalkModule j z
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_span_range_stalk_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
    (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf j) c hc z
  refine Stacks.Intersection.spanFinrank_ker_le_of_span_cotangent
    (j.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom (j.liftCoborder.stalkMap_surjective z) ?_
    (fun i => Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent j z (v i))
    (Stacks.Intersection.span_range_map_eq_top
      (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent j z) v hv)
  intro a m
  show (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective
    (j.liftCoborder.stalkMap_surjective z)).symm
      ((j.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom a) • m = a • m
  rw [RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_symm_apply, ← Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
  exact algebraMap_smul _ a m

/-- **The number of equations cutting out a regular immersion of codimension `c`.** If the
conormal sheaf of an immersion `j` into a locally Noetherian scheme is finite locally free of
rank `c`, then the kernel of `𝒪_{X, j z} ⟶ 𝒪_{Z,z}` needs at most `c` generators. -/
theorem spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_le_of_conormal_rank {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (j : Z ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion j] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (c : ℕ)
    [SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf j) c]
    (z : Z) : (RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank ≤ c := by
  have hfg : j = j.liftCoborder ≫ j.coborderRange.ι := j.liftCoborder_ι.symm
  let e : X.presheaf.stalk (j z) ≃+*
      j.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (j.liftCoborder.base z) :=
    (X.presheaf.stalkCongr
      (.of_eq (congrArg (fun q : Z ⟶ X => q z) hfg))).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.trans
      (asIso (j.coborderRange.ι.stalkMap (j.liftCoborder.base z))).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  have hmap : (j.stalkMap z).hom = (j.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom.comp e.toRingHom := by
    conv_lhs => rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_congr_hom j (j.liftCoborder ≫ j.coborderRange.ι) hfg z]
    rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp]
    rfl
  have hker : RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap z).hom =
      Ideal.map e.symm (RingHom.ker (j.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom) := by
    rw [hmap, ← RingHom.comap_ker, Ideal.map_symm]
    rfl
  rw [hker, Ideal.spanFinrank_map_eq_of_ringEquiv]
  exact spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_le_of_conormal_rank j c z

/-! ### The inverse image of a subvariety under a regular immersion -/

/-- The inverse image of `g : Z ⟶ Y` under an immersion `f : X ⟶ Y` is the fibre product of the
closed factor of `f` with the inverse image of `g` in the coborder neighbourhood of `f`. -/
private noncomputable def pullbackImmersionFactorizationIso {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    [IsImmersion f] (g : Z ⟶ Y) :
    (pullback f.liftCoborder (pullback.fst f.coborderRange.ι g) : Scheme.{u}) ≅
      (pullback f g : Scheme.{u}) :=
  (pullbackRightPullbackFstIso f.coborderRange.ι g f.liftCoborder) ≪≫
    eqToIso (congrArg (fun h : X ⟶ Y => (pullback h g : Scheme.{u})) f.liftCoborder_ι)

/-- An isomorphism of schemes matches up the irreducible components, preserving dimensions. -/
private lemma exists_component_iso_dim_eq {P Q : Scheme.{u}} (e : P ≅ Q) (W : Set Q)
    (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents Q) :
    ∃ V : Set P, V ∈ irreducibleComponents P ∧
      topologicalKrullDim V = topologicalKrullDim W := by
  let h := Scheme.homeoOfIso e
  refine ⟨h ⁻¹' W, preimage_mem_irreducibleComponents hW h.isOpenEmbedding ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hW.1.1
    exact ⟨y, hy, ⟨h.symm y, h.apply_symm_apply _⟩⟩
  · exact (h.subtype (fun _ => Iff.rfl)).isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq

/-- An irreducible component of a scheme that meets an open subscheme restricts to an
irreducible component of that open subscheme, of no larger dimension. -/
private lemma exists_component_preimage_dim_le {P Q : Scheme.{u}} (j : P ⟶ Q)
    [IsOpenImmersion j] (W : Set Q) (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents Q)
    (hne : (W ∩ Set.range j.base).Nonempty) :
    ∃ V : Set P, V ∈ irreducibleComponents P ∧
      topologicalKrullDim V ≤ topologicalKrullDim W :=
  ⟨j.base ⁻¹' W, preimage_mem_irreducibleComponents hW j.isOpenEmbedding hne,
    (j.isOpenEmbedding.isInducing.restrictPreimage W).topologicalKrullDim_le⟩

/-- A nonempty open subscheme of an irreducible scheme locally of finite type over a field has
the dimension of the whole scheme. -/
@[sga "3 VIB 1.5" "more general"]
private lemma topologicalKrullDim_eq_of_isOpenImmersion (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {U Z : Scheme.{u}} (s : Z ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] [IrreducibleSpace Z]
    (j : U ⟶ Z) [IsOpenImmersion j] [Nonempty U] :
    topologicalKrullDim U = topologicalKrullDim Z := by
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_eq_of_isOpen k Z s (Set.range j.base)
    j.isOpenEmbedding.isOpen_range (Set.range_nonempty _)]
  exact j.isEmbedding.toHomeomorph.isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq

/-- **The dimension of the components of the inverse image of a subvariety under an immersion
cut out by `c` equations.** Let `A` be a scheme locally of finite type over a field, let
`f : X ⟶ A` be an immersion from a quasi-compact scheme whose conormal sheaf is finite locally
free of rank `c`, and let `i : B ⟶ A` be a closed immersion with `B` integral. Then every
irreducible component `W` of `f⁻¹(B) = X ×_A B` satisfies `dim B ≤ dim W + c`. -/
theorem topologicalKrullDim_le_component_pullback_add_of_conormal_rank
    (k : Type u) [Field k] {X A B : Scheme.{u}} (sA : A ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sA] (f : X ⟶ A) [IsImmersion f] [CompactSpace X] (c : ℕ)
    [SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf f) c]
    (i : B ⟶ A) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsIntegral B]
    (W : Set (pullback f i : Scheme.{u}))
    (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents (pullback f i : Scheme.{u})) :
    topologicalKrullDim B ≤ topologicalKrullDim W + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  let Q : Scheme.{u} := pullback f.coborderRange.ι i
  let qA : Q ⟶ f.coborderRange.toScheme := pullback.fst f.coborderRange.ι i
  let qB : Q ⟶ B := pullback.snd f.coborderRange.ι i
  let P : Scheme.{u} := pullback qA f.liftCoborder
  let e : P ≅ (pullback f i : Scheme.{u}) :=
    pullbackSymmetry qA f.liftCoborder ≪≫ pullbackImmersionFactorizationIso f i
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hVdim⟩ := exists_component_iso_dim_eq e W hW
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hV.1.1
  have : Nonempty P := ⟨v⟩
  have : Nonempty Q := ⟨(pullback.fst qA f.liftCoborder).base v⟩
  have : IsIntegral Q := isIntegral_of_isOpenImmersion qB
  let sB : B ⟶ Spec (.of k) := i ≫ sA
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType sB := inferInstance
  let sQ : Q ⟶ Spec (.of k) := qB ≫ sB
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType sQ := inferInstance
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian A := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian sA
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian f.coborderRange.toScheme :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (f.coborderRange.ι ≫ sA)
  have : CompactSpace (pullback f i : Scheme.{u}) :=
    (show IsClosedImmersion (pullback.fst f i) from
      inferInstance).isClosedEmbedding.compactSpace
  have : CompactSpace P := (Scheme.homeoOfIso e).symm.compactSpace
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (pullback.fst qA f.liftCoborder ≫ sQ) := inferInstance
  have : IsNoetherian P :=
    isNoetherian_of_compact_ofFiniteType (pullback.fst qA f.liftCoborder ≫ sQ)
  calc topologicalKrullDim B
      = topologicalKrullDim Q := (topologicalKrullDim_eq_of_isOpenImmersion k sB qB).symm
    _ ≤ topologicalKrullDim V + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
        topologicalKrullDim_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_add k sQ
          (pullback.fst qA f.liftCoborder) V hV c
          (spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_pullback_fst_le qA f.liftCoborder c
            (spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_le_of_conormal_rank f c))
    _ = topologicalKrullDim W + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) := by rw [hVdim]

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0AZN, part (1).** Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of varieties over a
field which is a regular immersion of codimension `c`, and let `Z ⊆ Y` be a closed subvariety.
Then every irreducible component `W` of the scheme-theoretic inverse image `f⁻¹(Z) = X ×_Y Z`
satisfies `dim Z ≤ dim W + c`, that is, has dimension at least `dim Z - c`.

This is the first of the two bounds of Tag 0AZN, under the hypotheses the source gives that
bound. The tag is registered on the statement of both bounds,
`AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback_bounds`. -/
theorem topologicalKrullDim_le_component_pullback_add_of_isRegularImmersion
    (k : Type u) [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [IsVariety k sX] [IsVariety k sY] (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsImmersion f] (hf : f ≫ sY = sX)
    (hreg : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsRegularImmersion f) (c : ℕ)
    [SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf f) c]
    (I : Y.IdealSheafData) [IsIntegral I.subscheme]
    (W : Set (pullback f I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u}))
    (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents (pullback f I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u})) :
    topologicalKrullDim I.subscheme ≤ topologicalKrullDim W + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace sX
  exact topologicalKrullDim_le_component_pullback_add_of_conormal_rank
    k sY f c I.subschemeι W hW

/-! ### Affine space over a variety -/

/-- Affine space on a finite index set over a field has dimension the number of coordinates. -/
private lemma topologicalKrullDim_affineSpace_field (k : Type u) [Field k] (J : Type u)
    [Fintype J] :
    topologicalKrullDim (AffineSpace J (Spec (.of k))) = (Fintype.card J : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  rw [(Scheme.homeoOfIso (AffineSpace.SpecIso J (.of k))).isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq]
  show topologicalKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum (MvPolynomial J k)) = _
  rw [PrimeSpectrum.topologicalKrullDim_eq_ringKrullDim,
    MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_of_isNoetherianRing, ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_field]
  simp

/-- Affine space is stable under base change. -/
private noncomputable def affineSpaceBaseChangeIso (J : Type u) {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (g : Z ⟶ Y) :
    (pullback ((AffineSpace J Y) ↘ Y) g : Scheme.{u}) ≅ AffineSpace J Z :=
  (pullbackSymmetry _ _) ≪≫
    (pullbackRightPullbackFstIso (terminal.from Y)
      (terminal.from (Spec (.of (MvPolynomial J (ULift ℤ))))) g) ≪≫
    eqToIso (congrArg
      (fun f : Z ⟶ _ => (pullback f (terminal.from
        (Spec (.of (MvPolynomial J (ULift ℤ))))) : Scheme.{u}))
      (Subsingleton.elim (g ≫ terminal.from Y) (terminal.from Z)))

/-- Affine space on a finite index set over a scheme locally of finite type over a field has the
dimension of the base plus the number of coordinates. -/
private lemma topologicalKrullDim_affineSpace (k : Type u) [Field k] (J : Type u) [Fintype J]
    (Z : Scheme.{u}) (s : Z ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] :
    topologicalKrullDim (AffineSpace J Z) =
      topologicalKrullDim Z + (Fintype.card J : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  calc topologicalKrullDim (AffineSpace J Z)
      = topologicalKrullDim (pullback ((AffineSpace J (Spec (.of k))) ↘ Spec (.of k)) s :
          Scheme.{u}) :=
        (Scheme.homeoOfIso (affineSpaceBaseChangeIso J s)).isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq.symm
    _ = topologicalKrullDim (AffineSpace J (Spec (.of k))) + topologicalKrullDim Z :=
        topologicalKrullDim_pullback k _ s
    _ = topologicalKrullDim Z + (Fintype.card J : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
        rw [topologicalKrullDim_affineSpace_field]
        exact add_comm _ _

/-- A scheme isomorphic to an integral scheme is integral. -/
private lemma isIntegral_of_iso {A B : Scheme.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) [IsIntegral B] : IsIntegral A := by
  rw [isIntegral_iff_irreducibleSpace_and_isReduced]
  exact ⟨e.hom.homeomorph.irreducibleSpace_iff.mpr inferInstance,
    isReduced_of_isOpenImmersion e.hom⟩

/-! ### Finiteness of the dimensions involved -/

/-- The closure of a point of a scheme locally of finite type over a field has dimension a
natural number: it is the transcendence degree of the residue field there. -/
private lemma exists_topologicalKrullDim_closure_eq_natCast (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {T : Scheme.{u}} (s : T ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] (x : T) :
    ∃ m : ℕ, topologicalKrullDim (closure ({x} : Set T)) = (m : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  let : Algebra k (T.residueField x) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ s.appTop ≫ T.Γevaluation x).hom.toAlgebra
  have : FinTrdeg k (T.residueField x) := residueField_finTrdeg k s x
  refine ⟨(Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg k (T.residueField x))).toNat, ?_⟩
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_closure_singleton_eq_trdeg k T s x]
  exact_mod_cast (ENat.natCast_toNat
    (ne_of_lt ((Cardinal.toENat_lt_top).2 (trdeg_lt_aleph0 k (T.residueField x))))).symm

/-- An irreducible component of a scheme locally of finite type over a field has dimension a
natural number. -/
private lemma exists_topologicalKrullDim_component_eq_natCast (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {T : Scheme.{u}} (s : T ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] (W : Set T)
    (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents T) :
    ∃ m : ℕ, topologicalKrullDim W = (m : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_topologicalKrullDim_closure_eq_natCast k s hW.1.genericPoint
  refine ⟨m, ?_⟩
  rwa [hW.1.isGenericPoint_genericPoint
    (isClosed_of_mem_irreducibleComponents W hW)] at hm

/-- An irreducible scheme locally of finite type over a field has dimension a natural
number. -/
private lemma exists_topologicalKrullDim_eq_natCast_of_irreducible (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {T : Scheme.{u}} (s : T ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType s] [IrreducibleSpace T] :
    ∃ m : ℕ, topologicalKrullDim T = (m : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_topologicalKrullDim_component_eq_natCast k s Set.univ
    (by rw [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton]; exact rfl)
  exact ⟨m, ((Homeomorph.Set.univ T).isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq).symm.trans hm⟩

/-! ### Local complete intersection morphisms of a given relative dimension -/

/-- A morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` is a **local complete intersection morphism of relative dimension
`r`** if every point of `X` has an open neighbourhood `U` over which `f` factors as a
Koszul-regular immersion `i : U ⟶ 𝐀^J_Y` followed by the projection, and if in every such
factorization the conormal sheaf of `i` is finite locally free of rank `#J - r`.

The relative dimension is an integer, negative for a regular immersion. -/
def IsLocalCompleteIntersectionOfRelativeDimension {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (r : ℤ) :
    Prop :=
  (∀ x : X, ∃ (J : Type u) (_ : Fintype J) (U : X.Opens) (_ : x ∈ U)
      (i : U.toScheme ⟶ AffineSpace J Y) (hi : IsImmersion i),
      letI : IsImmersion i := hi
      Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsKoszulRegularImmersion i ∧
        U.ι ≫ f = i ≫ ((AffineSpace J Y) ↘ Y)) ∧
    (∀ (J : Type u) [Fintype J] (U : X.Opens) (i : U.toScheme ⟶ AffineSpace J Y)
      (hi : IsImmersion i),
      letI : IsImmersion i := hi
      Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsKoszulRegularImmersion i →
        U.ι ≫ f = i ≫ ((AffineSpace J Y) ↘ Y) →
          ∃ c : ℕ, SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
            (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) c ∧ ((Fintype.card J : ℤ) = r + c))

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0AZN, part (2).** Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of varieties over a
field which is a local complete intersection morphism of relative dimension `r`, and let
`Z ⊆ Y` be a closed subvariety, of dimension `d`. Then every irreducible component `W` of the
scheme-theoretic inverse image `f⁻¹(Z) = X ×_Y Z` has dimension `m ≥ d + r`; both dimensions
are natural numbers.

This is the second of the two bounds of Tag 0AZN, under the hypotheses the source gives that
bound. The tag is registered on the statement of both bounds,
`AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback_bounds`. -/
theorem exists_add_relativeDimension_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback
    (k : Type u) [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [IsVariety k sX] [IsVariety k sY] (f : X ⟶ Y) (hf : f ≫ sY = sX) (r : ℤ)
    (hlci : IsLocalCompleteIntersectionOfRelativeDimension f r)
    (I : Y.IdealSheafData) [IsIntegral I.subscheme]
    (W : Set (pullback f I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u}))
    (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents (pullback f I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u})) :
    ∃ d m : ℕ, topologicalKrullDim I.subscheme = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧
      topologicalKrullDim W = (m : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧ (d : ℤ) + r ≤ (m : ℤ) := by
  let T : Scheme.{u} := pullback f I.subschemeι
  let sI : I.subscheme ⟶ Spec (.of k) := I.subschemeι ≫ sY
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType sI := inferInstance
  have : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace sX
  have : IsClosedImmersion (pullback.fst f I.subschemeι) := inferInstance
  let sT : T ⟶ Spec (.of k) := pullback.fst f I.subschemeι ≫ sX
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType sT := inferInstance
  have : CompactSpace T :=
    (show IsClosedImmersion (pullback.fst f I.subschemeι) from
      inferInstance).isClosedEmbedding.compactSpace
  have : IsNoetherian T := isNoetherian_of_compact_ofFiniteType sT
  have : IsNoetherian X := isNoetherian_of_compact_ofFiniteType sX
  obtain ⟨x, -, hxW, -⟩ :=
    exists_closed_point_mem_unique_irreducibleComponent k T sT W hW
  obtain ⟨J, hJ, U, hxU, i, hi, hkos, hfac⟩ := hlci.1 ((pullback.fst f I.subschemeι).base x)
  let : Fintype J := hJ
  have : IsImmersion i := hi
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hcard⟩ := hlci.2 J U i hi hkos hfac
  have : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
    (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) c := hc
  let o : (pullback U.ι (pullback.fst f I.subschemeι) : Scheme.{u}) ⟶ T :=
    pullback.snd U.ι (pullback.fst f I.subschemeι)
  have : IsOpenImmersion o := inferInstance
  have hxo : x ∈ Set.range o.base := by
    rw [IsOpenImmersion.range_pullbackSnd]
    simpa using hxU
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hVle⟩ := exists_component_preimage_dim_le o W hW ⟨x, hxW, hxo⟩
  let e₁ : (pullback U.ι (pullback.fst f I.subschemeι) : Scheme.{u}) ≅
      (pullback (U.ι ≫ f) I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u}) :=
    pullbackRightPullbackFstIso f I.subschemeι U.ι
  obtain ⟨V₁, hV₁, hV₁dim⟩ := exists_component_iso_dim_eq e₁.symm V hV
  let π : AffineSpace J Y ⟶ Y := (AffineSpace J Y) ↘ Y
  let Q : Scheme.{u} := pullback π I.subschemeι
  let q : Q ⟶ AffineSpace J Y := pullback.fst π I.subschemeι
  let e₂ : (pullback i q : Scheme.{u}) ≅ (pullback (U.ι ≫ f) I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u}) :=
    pullbackRightPullbackFstIso π I.subschemeι i ≪≫
      eqToIso (congrArg
        (fun a : U.toScheme ⟶ Y => (pullback a I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u})) hfac.symm)
  obtain ⟨V₂, hV₂, hV₂dim⟩ := exists_component_iso_dim_eq e₂ V₁ hV₁
  have : IsIntegral Q := isIntegral_of_iso (affineSpaceBaseChangeIso J I.subschemeι)
  have : IsClosedImmersion q := inferInstance
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (π ≫ sY) := inferInstance
  have : TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace U.toScheme :=
    U.ι.isOpenEmbedding.isInducing.noetherianSpace
  have : CompactSpace U.toScheme := inferInstance
  have hdimQ : topologicalKrullDim Q ≤ topologicalKrullDim V₂ + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    topologicalKrullDim_le_component_pullback_add_of_conormal_rank
      k (π ≫ sY) i c q V₂ hV₂
  have hdimQ' : topologicalKrullDim Q =
      topologicalKrullDim I.subscheme + (Fintype.card J : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    calc topologicalKrullDim Q
        = topologicalKrullDim (AffineSpace J I.subscheme) :=
          (Scheme.homeoOfIso
            (affineSpaceBaseChangeIso J I.subschemeι)).isHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq
      _ = _ := topologicalKrullDim_affineSpace k J I.subscheme sI
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_topologicalKrullDim_eq_natCast_of_irreducible k sI
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_topologicalKrullDim_component_eq_natCast k sT W hW
  refine ⟨d, m, hd, hm, ?_⟩
  have key : (d : WithBot ℕ∞) + (Fintype.card J : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤
      (m : WithBot ℕ∞) + (c : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    rw [← hd, ← hm, ← hdimQ']
    refine hdimQ.trans ?_
    rw [hV₂dim, hV₁dim]
    gcongr
  have hnat : d + Fintype.card J ≤ m + c := by exact_mod_cast key
  omega

/-! ### The whole of Stacks 0AZN -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0AZN.** Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of varieties over a field, let
`Z ⊆ Y` be a closed subvariety, presented by the ideal sheaf `I`, and let `W` be an irreducible
component of the scheme-theoretic inverse image `f⁻¹(Z) = X ×_Y Z`. Then:

1. if `f` is a regular immersion of codimension `c`, then `dim Z ≤ dim W + c`, that is, `W` has
   dimension at least `dim Z - c`;
2. if `f` is a local complete intersection morphism of relative dimension `r`, and `Z` has
   dimension `d`, then `W` has dimension `m` with `d + r ≤ m`.

Dimensions are `topologicalKrullDim`, valued in `WithBot ℕ∞`, which has no subtraction: the
source's `dim W ≥ d - c` in part (1) is accordingly a relation between the two dimensions,
`dim Z ≤ dim W + c`. In part (2) the relative dimension `r` is an integer, negative for a
regular immersion, so there the two dimensions are produced as the natural numbers they are and
`d + r ≤ m` is an inequality in `ℤ`. -/
@[stacks 0AZN "both bounds in one statement, for a morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` of varieties over a \
field, a closed subvariety `Z ⊆ Y` presented by an ideal sheaf, and `W` an irreducible component \
of the scheme-theoretic inverse image `f⁻¹(Z) = X ×_Y Z`. (1) when `f` is a regular immersion \
whose conormal sheaf is finite locally free of rank `c` — the source's codimension — \
`dim Z ≤ dim W + c`; (2) when `f` is a local complete intersection morphism of relative \
dimension `r`, in the sense of \
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsLocalCompleteIntersectionOfRelativeDimension`, `d + r ≤ m` for `d = dim Z` \
and `m = dim W`. The regular-immersion data of (1) and the local complete intersection data of \
(2) are the source's own, and each binds inside its own clause, as in the source. Dimensions are \
`topologicalKrullDim`, valued in `WithBot ℕ∞`, which has no subtraction, so the source's \
`dim W ≥ d - c` is spelled as the relation `dim Z ≤ dim W + c`; in (2) the relative dimension is \
an integer and may be negative, so the two dimensions are produced as the natural numbers they \
are — both are transcendence degrees of residue fields over the base field — and `d + r ≤ m` is \
an inequality in `ℤ`. The two bounds are \
`AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDim_le_component_pullback_add_of_isRegularImmersion` and \
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_add_relativeDimension_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback`."]
theorem topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback_bounds
    (k : Type u) [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [IsVariety k sX] [IsVariety k sY] (f : X ⟶ Y) (hf : f ≫ sY = sX)
    (I : Y.IdealSheafData) [IsIntegral I.subscheme]
    (W : Set (pullback f I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u}))
    (hW : W ∈ irreducibleComponents (pullback f I.subschemeι : Scheme.{u})) :
    (∀ [IsImmersion f], Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsRegularImmersion f →
        ∀ (c : ℕ) [SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
          (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf f) c],
          topologicalKrullDim I.subscheme ≤ topologicalKrullDim W + (c : WithBot ℕ∞)) ∧
      (∀ r : ℤ, IsLocalCompleteIntersectionOfRelativeDimension f r →
        ∃ d m : ℕ, topologicalKrullDim I.subscheme = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧
          topologicalKrullDim W = (m : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧ (d : ℤ) + r ≤ (m : ℤ)) := by
  refine ⟨fun hreg c => ?_, fun r hlci => ?_⟩
  · exact topologicalKrullDim_le_component_pullback_add_of_isRegularImmersion k sX sY f hf hreg c
      I W hW
  · exact exists_add_relativeDimension_le_topologicalKrullDim_component_pullback k sX sY f hf r
      hlci I W hW

end AlgebraicGeometry

